{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":1163,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:Hab.1","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"Habakkuk","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"Habakkuk 1","reference":"Habakkuk 1","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"The prophet complains of the violence practiced by the Jews, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":2,"text":"1-4.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":3,"text":"God foretells the punishment of it, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":4,"text":"5-11.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":5,"text":"The prophet complains of the mischief done by the Chaldeans, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":6,"text":"12-17.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":7,"text":"1.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":8,"text":"The burden - The prophet seems to speak of these grievous things, as a burden which he himself groaned under.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":9,"text":"4.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":10,"text":"Therefore - Because the wicked go on with impunity.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":11,"text":"The law - The whole law, moral, ceremonial, and judicial.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":12,"text":"Is slacked - Is slighted, and not observed.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":13,"text":"Go forth - From magistrates, Judges, and public officers.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":14,"text":"Doth compass about - As it were besieges, with design to oppress and ruin.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":15,"text":"5.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":16,"text":"Behold ye - Here God begins to answer the prophet.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":17,"text":"Among the heathen - See what judgments have been executed upon the heathen for like sins.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":18,"text":"6.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":19,"text":"Bitter - Cruel, and without mercy.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":20,"text":"Hasty - Speedy in executing their merciless purposes.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":21,"text":"7.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":22,"text":"Their judgment - The law they observe, is their own will.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":23,"text":"Their dignity - Their authority is all from themselves, without respect to any other law or rule whatever.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":24,"text":"8.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":25,"text":"The evening wolves - Which with fasting in the day, came out in the evening, fierce and ravenous.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":26,"text":"Shall spread - All over the land.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":27,"text":"9.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":28,"text":"For violence - To enrich themselves by making a prey of all.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":29,"text":"Their faces - Their very countenances shall be as blasting as the east-wind.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":30,"text":"10.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":31,"text":"At the kings - Which opposed their designs.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":32,"text":"And take it - By mighty mounts cast up.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":33,"text":"12.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":34,"text":"Shall not die - Be utterly destroyed.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":35,"text":"Ordained - Set up, and designed.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":36,"text":"Them - The Chaldean kingdom.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":37,"text":"For judgment - To execute this judgment, which is tempered with mercy.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":38,"text":"For correction - To chastise, not to destroy.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":39,"text":"14.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":40,"text":"And makest - Not infusing cruel appetites, but permitting them to act according to such appetite which was already in them.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":41,"text":"As the fishes - Of which the greater greedily devour the smaller.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":42,"text":"Creeping things - Which in the waters are food for the lesser fry; so the world, like the sea, is wholly oppression.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":43,"text":"No ruler - None to defend the weak, or restrain the mighty.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":44,"text":"15.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":15,"scriptureVerseEnd":15},{"verse":45,"text":"They - The Chaldeans draw out all alike, good or bad.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":15,"scriptureVerseEnd":15},{"verse":46,"text":"In their net - Destroying many together.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":15,"scriptureVerseEnd":15},{"verse":47,"text":"And gather - As if they could never have enough, they drive men into their nets.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":15,"scriptureVerseEnd":15},{"verse":48,"text":"16.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16},{"verse":49,"text":"They sacrifice - Ascribe the praise of their victories.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16},{"verse":50,"text":"Their net - To their own contrivances, diligence, and power.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16},{"verse":51,"text":"17.","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":52,"text":"Empty their net - As fisher-men empty the full net to fill it again.","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Habakkuk","chapter":1}}